  "repairs": [
    "YEAR applies source warning policy before adjustment, stops with zero on fatal conversion and reports adjustment error1264. JSON uses caller flags.",
    "ENUM/SET parse numeric results only after handled source diagnostics; preserve earlier warnings, zero sentinels and SQL cause1265. ENUM uses its own unsigned bound.",
    "BIT performs source conversion before width validation, retains warnings and gives width1406 precedence over source errors. Invalid vector conversion retains zero; SET retains NULL; failed numeric YEAR retains zero, all with plain SQL fallback1105.",
    "Every table caller shares contextual conversion; ENUM/SET are excluded from generic1265 retitling. INSERT/UPDATE/ODKU and generated ODKU retain their completion rules.",
    "Warning value text delegates to shared Datum.ToString bytes, including ENUM/SET names. Context creation in the legacy interface is limited to the four migrated targets."
  ],
  "removals": [
    "Legacy table value/event conversion fallback and its error reconstruction",
    "Conditional contextual-cast admission matrix",
    "Separate generated/ordinary ODKU fallback and warning rewrite",
    "StmtContext.rewrite_warnings_from (last caller migrated)",
    "Duplicate datum_error_text scalar formatter; keep only the existing UTF-8 projection adapter",
    "Private convert_to_signed/convert_to_unsigned wrappers, year_from_text and value_to_literal_uint"
  ],
  "retained": "conversion_event_is_silent remains for three DDL callers. No tests were removed merely for exposing a failure. Existing neighboring regressions remain.",
